# Tl - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Tl.ugur Tl
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -4.75 meV (0.186 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against the measured dispersion the hard sets average 9.7 % over the 33 elements that have one, against 12.6 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 25 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 330 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Tl at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Tl Tl Tl 3.8719818301361051 0.57351497711911581 0.8803604169143523 3.2120167762021392 2.7625800303805615e-07 -0.40110409778058886 0.61764059823303208 8.9960000000000004 5.1106066176139988 -1 0 0
